/*
 * Preflight - the baseline every utility outranks.
 *
 * Tailwind v4's preflight zeroes margin and padding on every element. UI Toolkit's own controls give a Label
 * a margin and padding of their own, and Velvet resets that one: `unity-label` is the class a Label is
 * constructed with. The rule is imported ahead of every utility sheet, so a `p-*` or `m-*` on the same
 * element ties with it on specificity and wins on order.
 *
 * The generator's utility table skips a `unity-` selector (UssSelectorKind.EngineClass), so this baseline
 * never counts as a class declaring its own margin or padding.
 */

.unity-label { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
